From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ryan Stoffel <stoffel.thomas.ryan@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 21:28:24 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] workbench: load wisp in the Agents window

The Agents window is a separate workbench. Its entry point,
sessions.desktop.main.ts, never imports workbench.desktop.main.ts, so
the editor window's wisp contribution never runs there.

src/vs/sessions/contrib/wisp/browser/wisp.sessions.contribution.ts comes
from the overlay and is wisp's entry point in this window, the way
wisp.contribution.ts is in the editor window. wisp's sessions provider
and sidebar view are imported from it without another patch.

The import goes last, after every upstream contribution it adjusts.

diff --git a/src/vs/sessions/sessions.desktop.main.ts b/src/vs/sessions/sessions.desktop.main.ts
index 15b895783966169aa4c2d012a1c76f5e4a190a4e..c0c5713ec3b51071e96e7b2c57aea5eebb261195 100644
--- a/src/vs/sessions/sessions.desktop.main.ts
+++ b/src/vs/sessions/sessions.desktop.main.ts
@@ -265,6 +265,9 @@ import './contrib/tunnelHost/electron-browser/tunnelHost.contribution.js';
 // Sessions (desktop only)
 import './contrib/sessions/electron-browser/sessions.contribution.js';
 
+// wisp
+import './contrib/wisp/browser/wisp.sessions.contribution.js';
+
 //#endregion
 
 export { main } from './electron-browser/sessions.main.js';
